{
  "_comment": "SHARED CONFORMANCE VECTORS -- FROZEN. Read byte-identically by govder/internal/oversight (Go) and vultrino/src/approval (Rust). They pin approval-recipe SATISFACTION, which is implemented TWICE on purpose (govder recipeSatisfied / vultrino recipe_satisfied) and has already diverged once. A failing row is a CROSS-PLANE DIVERGENCE: govder and vultrino now disagree about whether an approval is complete. Do NOT regenerate this file to make a test pass.",
  "_shared_copies": [
    "govder/internal/oversight/testdata/recipe_vectors.json",
    "vultrino/src/approval/testdata/recipe_vectors.json"
  ],
  "_contract": "satisfied(recipe, avail) is the COMPOSED contract each plane must implement: (1) a structurally malformed recipe (empty, count outside [1,64], summed total > 64, unknown class) is permanently unsatisfiable; (2) any agent-reviewer term makes the recipe unsatisfiable regardless of availability (system-wide disable); (3) otherwise an INJECTIVE sign-off -> slot matching must exist, where a senior may fill a senior OR a teammate slot, a teammate only a teammate slot, and an agent-reviewer only an agent-reviewer slot. Rust folds (1) into recipe_satisfied via recipe_well_formed. Go does NOT: govder's recipeSatisfied assumes its caller already dropped malformed recipes (evaluateApprovalRule's validRecipes filter, via recipeFloorOK -> recipeComposition). go_raw_satisfied records what govder's recipeSatisfied returns WITHOUT that filter -- it is pinned so the precondition can never be quietly removed, and the rows where it differs from `satisfied` are exactly the load-bearing ones.",
  "_domain": "MAX_RECIPE_TERM_COUNT = 64 bounds both the per-term count and the summed total, so the recipe side of this contract is a FINITE domain and the sweeps below are EXHAUSTIVE over it, not samples. See each sweep's own `exhaustive_over` / `sampled_over` fields for exactly which axes are which.",
  "cap": 64,
  "u32_max": 4294967295,
